Reload the IPF rules.

ipf -Fa -A -f /etc/ipf/ipf.conf

For Solaris 11.3 or newer that use Packet Filter remove or modify any rules that include \"allow-opts\".

Reload the Packet Filter rules:svcadm refresh firewall:default"
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216157r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-050370,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216157"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
          cmd         : "/usr/sbin/pfctl -s rules | /usr/bin/grep allow-opts | /usr/bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
